<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malazgirt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malazgirt is a town in Muş Province in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-van">Lake Van</a>, known in Byzantine and medieval sources as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-manzikert">Manzikert</a>. It lies in the ancient Urartian and Armenian highlands on routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. In 1071 the Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alp-arslan">Alp Arslan</a> defeated the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-iv-diogenes">Romanos IV Diogenes</a> nearby, opening Anatolia to Turkish settlement.</p></div>
